
AOMP is a build of the ROCm stack for the compiler development team.
AOMP uses TheRock to build all ROCm components from source.
AOMP is different than building the tip of TheRock in 2 ways.

1) AOMP builds the main branch of TheRock on a specific frozen hash
   key associated with the next release of the AOMP compiler. This
   TheRock hash key implies a set of hash keys for each of TheRock
   submodules with the exception of submodule amd-llvm and hipify.
2) The submodules at compiler/amd-llvm and compiler/hipify use the
   latest amd-staging branches which is the integration branch for
    compiler development.

This directory (aomp/tr_aomp) contains all the support to build AOMP
using TheRock.

The current two-step build process is:

1) ./tr_clone_aomp.sh
2) ./tr_build_aomp.sh

On first execution, tr_clone_aomp.sh will clone TheRock repo which 
has many submodules. The submodule branches for compiler/amd-llvm and 
compiler/hipify are overridden to use the latest amd-staging branch.
Subsequent executions of tr_clone_aomp.sh will pull the latest updates
to the amd-staging branch for compiler/amd-llvm and compiler/hipify 
and pull the latest updates to aomp-dev of the aomp repository.

The default for the env variable TR_AOMP_REPOS is /work/$USER/git/tr-aomp.
tr_clone_aomp.sh clones TheRock repo into $TR_AOMP_REPOS/TheRock
and initialize it. It is important to set the environment variable 
if the default does not exist.  tr_clone_aomp.sh will clone the aomp
repo to $TR_AOMP_REPOS/aomp and pull most recent updates.

It is always safe to run or rerun tr_clone_aomp.sh. Typically, all that
happens are updates to amd-staging branch of llvm-project and hipify.

New AOMP Release Management by AOMP Release Manager
===================================================
Every aomp release has an info file stored in aomp_<RELEASE>/<RELEASE>.info
It is rare that no info file exists.  This only occurs when the release
manager starts a new AOMP release.  Most developers will use the info file
provided by the release manager at the beginning of an AOMP release.
If no info file is present, the build process will initialize a new
AOMP release by creating the info file for the release with the current
tip of TheRock repo. Subsequent builds will remain on the shakey
found when the release is initialized.  Creating new AOMP releases will
be how the AOMP team keeps pace with TheRock while insulating developers
from other ROCm development churn. Of course, AOMP developers are always
exposed to the churn in the llvm-project compiler repository.

Any changes or fixes to TheRock repo or its submodules during the development
of the AOMP release, can be shared with the team by creating a set of patches
with the script tr_create_patch.sh.

tr_build_aomp.sh builds ROCm into $TR_AOMP_REPOS/TheRock/build/dist/rocm.
using the standard TheRock build process with cmake and ninja.
Then copies using rsync from $TR_AOMP_REPOS/TheRock/build/dist/rocm 
to $AOMP_INSTALL_DIR.

These two symlinks help to iterate development of llvm-project. 
ln -sf $TR_AOMP_REPOS/TheRock/compiler/amd-llvm $TR_AOMP_REPOS/llvm-project
ln -sf $TR_AOMP_REPOS/TheRock/build/compiler/amd-llvm/build $TR_AOMP_REPOS/llvm-project/build

Compiler Development Flow: 
--------------------------
The flow has three phases, initialize, iterate, and promote.

INITIALIZE:
  - run tr_clone_aomp.sh
  - run tr_build_aomp.sh

ITERATE:
  EDIT
    - cd git/tr-aomp/llvm-project 
      The above is a symlink to git/tr-aomp/TheRock/compiler/amd-llvm
      which contains the llvm-project submodule. 
    - edit llvm-project files in the llvm source tree
  UPDATE AND INSTALL BUILD
    - run tr_build_aomp.sh restart
      Running without the restart option will create a fresh full build 
      which takes a very long time. 
  TEST
    - test with AOMP=$AOMP_INSTALL_DIR or
      AOMP=/work/$USER/rocm/tr-aomp which is a symlink to $AOMP_INSTALL_DIR
  MERGE updates, if necessary
   - run tr_clone_aomp.sh
     This will only update aomp, llvm-project, and hipify repos.

PROMOTE 
   MERGE any updates if necessary with tr_clone_aomp.sh
   TEST merged updates if necessary
   PROMOTE via a trunk PR or an amd-staging PR. 

Patching non-compiler Components
--------------------------------
Other than fixes made by AOMP release manager, it is rare for compiler
developers to fix components other than in llvm-project. If this occurs, 
and your fixes need to be shared with other developers, the script 
tr_create_patch.sh will update the set of patches for this release. 
Be sure to push or PR those patches to the aomp repo for sharing.

Environment Variables to Speed-up Builds
----------------------------------------

Set these environment variables to skip builds of ROCm components:

AOMP_SKIP_MATH_LIBS=1
AOMP_SKIP_COMPOSABLE_KERNEL=1
AOMP_SKIP_ML_LIBS=1
AOMP_SKIP_RCCL=1
AOMP_SKIP_FFT=1



